{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 22, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "**A Whirlwind Through Japan’s Wonders**\n\nStepping off the plane in Tokyo, the city’s neon glow and bustling energy wrapped around me like a familiar hug. Our first stop was **Shibuya Crossing**, where thousands moved in perfect sync—chaotic yet orderly. A quick bite at a tiny *izakaya* introduced me to melt-in-your-mouth yakitori, washed down with crisp sake.\n\nThe next morning, the **Meiji Shrine** offered a serene escape. Towering torii gates led to a forest altar, where prayer plaques fluttered in the breeze. A short train ride brought us to **Asakusa**, where the scent of *ningyo-yaki* (red bean cakes) mingled with temple incense at **Senso-ji**. We bought *omikuji* (fortune slips)—mine read *\"Great success ahead!\"*—before escaping to Ameya-Yokocho’s vibrant market.\n\nKyoto was pure magic. Wandering **Fushimi Inari’s** endless vermilion torii paths, I climbed until the shrine vanished beneath a sea of gates. **Arashiyama’s bamboo forest** whispered secrets as sunlight filtered through emerald stems. A tea ceremony at **Camellia Garden** taught me the art of slow sipping—matcha’s bittersweet depth lingered long after.\n\nOsaka’s **Dotonbori** was a foodcomatic explosion. Takoyaki sizzled on skewers, and the neon signs for **Kushikatsu** (deep-fried skewers) beckoned. We split a bowl of *okonomiyaki* (savory pancake) under a sign for **Kani Doraku**, its crab shape glowing like a promise.\n\nTokyo’s final evening found us at **Odaiba**, where teamLab Planets’ **Boundaryless** installation made us run through digital waterfalls. As cherry blossoms faded, I left with full heart—and already dreaming of returning.\n\nJapan isn’t just visited; it’s *experienced*. One trip feels like a teaser for the next.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.06550939381122589}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.27843376994132996}, {"token": " Wh", "lo